## Day 65 Session Plan

**3 tasks, all self-driven** (no sponsor issues, community issue #156 deferred — needs external coordination):

| # | Task | Type | Files |
|---|------|------|-------|
| 1 | Extract architect-mode turn + post-prompt handling from `run_repl` | Structural health | src/repl.rs |
| 2 | Add `/model info <name>` subcommand — show pricing, context window, provider for any model | Capability (competitive) | src/commands_info.rs, src/dispatch.rs, src/help.rs |
| 3 | Add `/history detail` subcommand — per-turn breakdown with tools used and token counts | Capability (competitive) | src/commands_session.rs, src/dispatch.rs, src/help.rs |

Rationale:
• **Task 1** tackles the single largest function in the codebase (985 lines). Extracting ~230 lines into two helper functions makes the REPL loop scannable and contributor-friendly.
• Task 2 fills a real user gap — when picking a model, you need to know what it costs and how much context it has. This info exists in the codebase but isn't exposed to users.
• Task 3 improves session introspection — /history currently shows bare role+preview. The detail view shows what tools were used per turn and how many tokens were consumed, helping users understand their context budget.

All three are well within the 20-minute budget and touch ≤3 files each. Tasks 2 and 3 both touch `dispatch.rs and help.rs` but in different sections (different match arms, different help blocks).

